sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant GW as API Gateway (Node 1)
    participant BG as Background Async Thread
    participant R as Central Redis Store

    Note over R: Global Limit: 1000/sec
    
    %% Initialization
    GW->>BG: Initialize Rate Limiter
    BG->>R: Reserve Batch (e.g., 100 tokens)
    R-->>BG: OK, 100 Reserved (900 remaining)
    BG->>GW: Update Local Cache (Tokens=100)
    
    %% Fast path
    C->>GW: Request 1
    Note over GW: Sub-microsecond check<br/>Tokens: 99
    GW-->>C: 200 OK
    
    C->>GW: Request N
    Note over GW: Tokens drop below threshold (e.g., < 20)
    GW-->>C: 200 OK
    
    %% Async Replenishment
    GW->>BG: Trigger Replenishment (Non-blocking)
    BG->>R: Reserve Next Batch (100 tokens)
    
    %% Continuous traffic during replenishment
    C->>GW: Request N+1
    Note over GW: Local tokens still available
    GW-->>C: 200 OK
    
    R-->>BG: OK, 100 Reserved (800 remaining)
    BG->>GW: Update Local Cache (Tokens += 100)
    
    %% Over limit scenario
    Note over R: Global Quota Exhausted (0 remaining)
    BG->>R: Reserve Next Batch
    R-->>BG: Rejected, Limit Exceeded
    BG->>GW: Cache Empty, Refill Failed
    
    C->>GW: Request (No local tokens)
    GW-->>C: 429 Too Many Requests
